 applied after a side effect, evaluated under the wrong identity or tenant, or unsupported by reproducible evidence.', limitations='This bounded ARL-KB-035 test does not prove absence of undiscovered paths, future regressions or risks outside the stated identities, inputs, environment and version.', content_digest='e3b62c853310f2529d1a223875641a4a7aee0b3d6f38fe79a9475f75ba61f963', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-035';
UPDATE risk_knowledge_solutions SET control_objective='Reduce the likelihood and impact of instruction priority is ambiguous and make the remaining risk visible.', recommended_remediation='Use typed message channels, preserve provenance, reject role spoofing and keep enforcement rules outside free-form context.', default_owner='AI application owner', priority='P1', implementation_principles_json='["ARL-KB-035: Preserve typed source provenance and explicit instruction hierarchy throughout context construction.","ARL-KB-035: Treat role names or policy claims appearing inside free-form content as data, not authority.","ARL-KB-035: Keep security-critical enforcement outside ambiguous natural-language precedence."]', monitoring='For ARL-KB-035, record policy version and digest, actor, target, decision, denial reason and side-effect outcome; alert the AI application owner on bypass attempts, configuration drift, repeated denials and missing decision evidence.', containment='Contain ARL-KB-035 by disabling the affected capability or route, revoking scoped authority, isolating impacted identities and data, preserving versioned evidence, and requiring owner approval before re-enablement.', retest_acceptance_json='["ARL-KB-035: “Instruction priority is ambiguous” is no longer reproducible against the exact remediated version.","ARL-KB-035: Authorised in-scope use completes successfully, remains within the documented asset scope for instruction priority is ambiguous, and produces no unintended side effect.","ARL-KB-035: Unauthorised identity, boundary-crossing, malformed-input, replay and relevant bypass variants are denied before execution, with the expected policy and downstream events recorded.","ARL-KB-035: Reviewer identity, timestamp, deployed version, evidence digest, known limitations and rollback decision are recorded."]', content_digest='57783fa8bfe8027aad0b39fafbf5dd5e7a31d480455175804615043c80bf15f1', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-035';
