le-tag drift or deployed-image mismatch evidence","ARL-KB-075 evidence expiry or material scope, architecture or assessed-version change"],"review_status":"expert-authored candidate; customer and independent practitioner validation required"}', content_digest='1fcdd83fc261f2e3872ee2b0185332c8e4ceae66081ba6fb09c275fba3d0d6be', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE id='ARL-KB-075';
UPDATE risk_knowledge_checks SET objective='Determine whether the exact container or runtime image assessed can be identified immutably and reproduced without silently resolving a mutable tag to different bytes.', method='Compare source build records, image manifest, immutable digest and the exact deployed runtime image. Resolve any mutable tag currently in use and test whether rebuilding or redeploying after upstream tag movement would produce different bytes from the assessed release.', check_types_json='["declared-control review","observed-control inspection","negative or abuse test","evidence review"]', required_evidence_json='["ARL-KB-075 assessed system, version, environment and scope for Container or runtime image uses a mutable tag","ARL-KB-075 control configuration or source location showing how reduce the likelihood and impact of container or runtime image uses a mutable tag and make the remaining risk visible.","ARL-KB-075 positive and abuse inputs with expected and observed outputs for agent and model context","ARL-KB-075 policy, authorization, tool or audit events proving whether the tested container or runtime image uses a mutable tag path executed","ARL-KB-075 tester identity, role, timestamp and evidence digest"]', pass_condition='ARL-KB-075 passes only when “Container or runtime image uses a mutable tag” is not reproducible through the documented abuse cases, the valid workflow remains bounded to agent and model context, denial occurs before side effects, and version-bound observed evidence matches the expected decision.', fail_condition='ARL-KB-075 fails when a rebuild can silently use different bytes than the assessed release, or when the relevant control is declaration-only, bypassable, fail-open, applied after a side effect, evaluated under the wrong identity or tenant, or unsupported by reproducible evidence.', limitations='This bounded ARL-KB-075 test does not prove absence of undiscovered paths, future regressions or risks outside the stated identities, inputs, environment and version.', content_digest='a42d617c7d3925357cc7e9d7d371003b33ac57aa7339b31ab1ac5e27d5893898', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-075';
UPDATE risk_knowledge_solutions SET control_objective='Reduce the likelihood and impact of container or runtime image uses a mutable tag and make the remaining risk visible.', recommended_remediation='Pin image digests, retain signed provenance and scan the exact deployed image; update through an explicit tested release.', default_owner='DevSecOps owner', priority='P1', implementation_principles_json='["ARL-KB-075: Reference production runtime images by immutable digest rather than mutable tags alone.","ARL-KB-075: Record build provenance and tie security evidence to the exact deployed image digest.","ARL-KB-075: Treat image-byte changes as a new release requiring explicit validation rather than silent replacement."]', monitoring='For ARL-KB-075, record policy version and digest, actor, target, decision, denial reason and side-effect outcome; alert the DevSecOps owner on bypass attempts, configuration drift, repeated denials and missing decision evidence.', containment='Contain ARL-KB-075 by disabling the affected capability or route, revoking scoped authority, isolating impacted identities and data, preserving versioned evidence, and requiring owner approval before re-enablement.', retest_acceptance_json='["ARL-KB-075: “Container or runtime image uses a mutable tag” is no longer reproducible against the exact remediated version.","ARL-KB-075: Authorised in-scope use completes successfully, remains within the documented asset scope for container or runtime image uses a mutable tag, and produces no unintended side effect.","ARL-KB-075: Unauthorised identity, boundary-crossing, malformed-input, replay and relevant bypass variants are denied before execution, with the expected policy and downstream events recorded.","ARL-KB-075: Reviewer identity, timestamp, deployed version, evidence digest, known limitations and rollback decision are recorded."]', content_digest='5761750a8db942ced9ccf175790d8edcc770e7d47e855f474dd1112e81ef106e', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-075';
